%N A400899 Number of isomorphism classes of connected simple Eulerian graphs on n vertices with a proper vertex coloring in red and blue, where isomorphisms preserve the colors.
%C A400899 Every edge joins vertices of different colors. The colors need not both occur.
%C A400899 Two colored graphs are equivalent if there is a graph isomorphism that maps red vertices to red vertices and blue vertices to blue vertices.
%F A400899 a(n) = Sum_{k|n} mu(k)/k * [x^(n/k)] log B(x), where
%F A400899 B(x) = (1+x)/(1-x) + Sum_{p,q>=1} x^(p+q) * Sum_{alpha partition of p, beta partition of q} 2^(G(alpha,beta)-l(alpha)-l(beta)+kappa(alpha,beta))/(z_alpha*z_beta).
%F A400899 For alpha = (alpha_1,...,alpha_r) and beta = (beta_1,...,beta_s), l(alpha) = r, l(beta) = s, and G(alpha,beta) = Sum_{i=1..r} Sum_{j=1..s} gcd(alpha_i,beta_j).
%F A400899 Define z_alpha = Product_{j>=1} (j^m_j(alpha) * m_j(alpha)!), where m_j(alpha) is the number of parts of alpha equal to j; define z_beta similarly.
%F A400899 Let u = min_i nu_2(alpha_i) and v = min_j nu_2(beta_j).
%F A400899 Then kappa(alpha,beta) = 1 if u = v; kappa(alpha,beta) = #{i: nu_2(alpha_i) < v} if u < v; and kappa(alpha,beta) = #{j: nu_2(beta_j) < u} if u > v.
%F A400899 Here nu_2(t) is the exponent of 2 in t.
%e A400899 For n = 1, the single vertex can be red or blue, giving a(1) = 2.
%e A400899 For n = 6, the underlying graphs are C_6 and K_{2,4}. The two proper colorings of C_6 are isomorphic by a color-preserving isomorphism between the colored graphs. The two proper colorings of K_{2,4} are not, since their red vertex sets have different sizes. Thus a(6) = 1 + 2 = 3.
%Y A400899 Cf. A243320.
